  "mic": "XLIS",
  "name": "Euronext Lisbon",
  "note": "2010-2024 sourced from exchange_calendars only (backfill; not independently verified). 2025-2027: exchange_calendars + exchange_publications (the exchange's calendar, published to 2027). 2028-2029: predicted from exchange_calendars and the exchange's unchanged pattern; not yet published, although most entries cite the calendar page. regular_hours are Lisbon local time (timezone Europe/Lisbon): 08:00-16:30. Euronext publishes its cash-market hours in CET (09:00-17:30; its Trading Procedures Annexe One says all hours are CET), and Lisbon is one hour behind CET. The registry had 09:00-17:30 under Europe/Lisbon, which is one hour late; exchange_calendars (08:00-16:30), tradinghours.com (08:00-16:30 WET) and the ICE Futures Europe year-end schedule (Euronext Lisbon stops 13:05 GMT on the half days) agree with the corrected value. Half-day early_close_time values are Lisbon local (13:05 = 14:05 CET). Rechecked 2026-11-19 (4c-R3) against Euronext's trading-hours-and-holidays page and its 2027 holiday calendar. Fixed: 2027-12-24 and 2027-12-31 are published half trading days and were missing; 2029-12-24 and 2029-12-31 added as predicted half days (exchange_calendars, XAMS, XPAR and XDUB have them). 2025-2027 closures match. Hours 09:00-17:30 CET throughout; the only 2027 change Euronext announces is Trading After Hours availability. No COVID-19 or other one-off closure in 2010-2024. Half-day time convention (4c-R3 decision: close = end of the closing auction): the half-day close 13:05 Lisbon (14:05 CET) is the end of the half-day closing auction (Euronext: all instruments close by 14:05 CET), so it follows the convention. The full-day close 16:30 Lisbon does not: since 2007-02-19 Euronext's continuous trading ends at 17:30 CET with the closing auction at 17:35 CET, so by the same convention the full-day close would be 16:35 Lisbon. Left unchanged here so that all Euronext core venues (XAMS, XPAR, XBRU, XLIS) change together; flagged for that change. Close convention (ADR 0013, 4c-R3.5): regular_hours close is the end of the closing auction, 16:35 Lisbon (17:35 CET), for 2010-2029 (was 16:30, the end of continuous trading). Source: Euronext's announcement of 2007-02-16 (effective 2007-02-19), reproduced by Mondo Visione: continuous trading 09:00-17:30 CET, pre-closing 17:30-17:35, closing auction at 17:35 CET; FESE trading-hours tables for 2024 and 2026 give the same (pre-closing 17:30-17:35, closing auction 17:35, Trading at Last 17:35-17:40). Half days close by 14:05 CET, also the auction end. exchange_calendars and pandas_market_calendars use the end of continuous trading, so session-time comparisons are a convention_difference.",
